I like to be heavily involved in all design discussions.

For each directory that starts with a number (for example, `0_KC`):

1. Read `CONTEXT` and `0_QUESTIONS`.
2. If a question has an answer clear enough to implement or discard, move it to `ANSWERED` and create a concrete TODO in `1_AGENT_TODOS` with a three-word title and brief subtitle. Do this only when the scope is clear and does not require guessing.
3. Complete TODOs in `1_AGENT_TODOS`, or answer questions placed there.
4. When an implementation choice is unclear, ask a question in `0_QUESTIONS` before coding. Err on the side of asking too many questions before coding, especially for design decisions.
5. For SQL changes, add a SQL file to `{{project}-api}/sql` for the user to run.
6. When adding a question, put it at the top under `UNANSWERED`, use a `-` bullet, and leave a blank tabbed response area after it.
7. Add a follow-up only after the original question has an answer. Indent it below the original as `- Follow Up:` and leave an indented response area after it.
8. When completing a user-facing feature, add it to the bottom of `FEATURES` using a three-word title, a colon, and a brief description.
9. Add user work, such as required secrets, to `2_TODOS`.
10. When completing an agent TODO, add a brief indented completion note and move it below active TODOs to the top of `DONE`. Do not add blank lines between done TODOs.
11. Finish by reading `0_QUESTIONS`, moving questions with a new follow-up to the top, and moving clearly answered questions to `ANSWERED`.

When done, run `git add .`, commit, and push for every repository touched.

All code outputs will be reviewed by Claude Code.
